sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant FE as Frontend
    participant API as FastAPI / WebSocket API
    participant RL as Command Rate Limit
    participant ENC as Command Encoder
    participant UDP as UDP Sender
    participant UAV as UAV / Planner
    participant WS as WebSocket Manager

    FE->>API: command / recording / PID request
    API->>RL: check channel busy + min interval

    alt rate limited
        RL-->>API: reject with retry_after
        API-->>FE: command_response(rate_limited)
    else accepted
        API->>ENC: encode NCLink packet
        ENC-->>API: bytes packet
        API->>UDP: send_data(packet, host, port)
        UDP-->>UAV: UDP command packet
        API-->>FE: command_response(success)
        opt state changed
            API->>WS: broadcast status snapshot
            WS-->>FE: config / recording / udp status update
        end
    end

    Note over FE,API: Frontend refresh only drops the browser-side connection.
    Note over API,UDP: UDP command channel remains alive independently of WebSocket lifecycle.
    Note over RL,ENC: Burst commands are serialized per channel to avoid internal congestion.